                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "21b11d29-a74e-319b-b137-04b51fa2d3f4",
                        "entry_id": "37674bbf-dde9-3a00-a925-3696c805d154",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A former dynasty in China, reigning from the end of the Yuan to the beginning of the Qing (Ching)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c24d147a-eb3a-4129-bfef-0037b5721058",
                                "sense_id": "21b11d29-a74e-319b-b137-04b51fa2d3f4",
                                "text": "CHWEN, King of Korea, having by his Ambaſſadors paid Homage to the Emperor Hong-vû, Founder of the Ming Dynaſty in 1368, was, by that Monarch, created King of Kau-li, preſented with a Silver Seal, and veſted with the ancient Privileges of ſacrificing to the Gods of the Rivers and Mountains of Korea."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c350055-44e8-4d9e-831a-295829adf323",
                                "sense_id": "21b11d29-a74e-319b-b137-04b51fa2d3f4",
                                "text": "The Comet of 1385 was discovered in China by the astronomers of the Ming dynasty, on October 23 (period Houng-wou eighteenth year, ninth moon, day Wou-yn): it was then on the borders of Thai-wei (a constellation of stars in Leo and Virgo, surrounding β Leonis); it touched β Virginis, and left Thai-wei by what the Chinese termed the \"great gate,\" i.e. between β and n Virginis."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30e0a39f-54f3-46c3-bfc4-9f275e88e464",
                                "sense_id": "21b11d29-a74e-319b-b137-04b51fa2d3f4",
                                "text": "When Koxinga, the Ming Dynasty loyalist who drove the Dutch colonists from Taiwan in 1661, ending an occupation that had laster 37 years, Taipei was nonexistent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e4553be-f91c-4636-be3e-08309dc48659",
                                "sense_id": "21b11d29-a74e-319b-b137-04b51fa2d3f4",
                                "text": "Only 8.2 percent of the wall, built during the Ming Dynasty (1368-1644) is maintained properly, according to a study by the China Great Wall Society, an organization dedicated to the preservation and protection of the Wall."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f565f52b-c1c7-4c69-9732-16c35fc28aa0",
                                "sense_id": "21b11d29-a74e-319b-b137-04b51fa2d3f4",
                                "text": "Among Professor Spence’s most ambitious books was “The Search for Modern China,” which made The New York Times’s best-seller list and is now a standard text. It took an 876-page view of China’s history from the decline of the Ming dynasty in the 1600s to the democracy movement of 1989."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8282af84-d586-3050-b0fd-59ccf26f8be9",
                        "entry_id": "37674bbf-dde9-3a00-a925-3696c805d154",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A former empire in China, occupying the eastern half of modern China (China proper), as well as parts of Russia and northern Vietnam"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "43a51cd2-ab09-3e9a-b827-a58df9b23f2c",
